---
import DetailLayout from "../../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---

<DetailLayout
  title="Songzanlin Monastery"
  description="Songzanlin Monastery, Shangri-La Yunnan: Yunnan's largest Tibetan Buddhist monastery (1679). Morning chanting, golden roofs, visitor tips, and etiquette."
  category="Attraction"
  image="songzanlin-monastery.webp"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "TouristAttraction",
    "name": "Songzanlin Monastery",
    "description": "The largest Tibetan Buddhist monastery in Yunnan, built in 1679 near Shangri-La. Known as the Little Potala Palace with stunning golden-roof architecture and daily morning chanting ceremonies.",
    "publicAccess": true
  }}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Songzanlin Monastery</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">The largest Tibetan Buddhist monastery in Yunnan. Built in 1679 and often called the Little Potala Palace. Morning chanting, golden roofs, and 700 monks in residence.</p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Altitude</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">3,300 m</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Time Needed</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">2&ndash;3 hrs</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Best Season</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">All Year</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Ticket</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">115 RMB</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Songzanlin Monastery (噶丹松赞林寺), also known as Guihua Monastery, was built in 1679 under the patronage of the Fifth Dalai Lama. It is the largest Tibetan Buddhist monastery in Yunnan Province and belongs to the Gelugpa (Yellow Hat) sect of Tibetan Buddhism. The architectural style is modeled after the Potala Palace in Lhasa, earning it the nickname "Little Potala Palace".</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The monastery complex sprawls across a hillside overlooking a sacred lake. At its peak, it housed over 2,000 monks. Today approximately 700 monks live and study here. The main assembly hall (Tsokchen) can hold 1,600 worshippers, with 108 red pillars supporting a golden roof visible from across the valley. Inside, Thangka paintings, butter lamp offerings, and towering gilded Buddha statues create an atmosphere of profound serenity.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The monastery is not a museum &mdash; it is a living religious institution. You will see young monks debating scriptures in the courtyard, elderly lamas circumambulating stupas with prayer beads, and locals prostrating before the main hall. The energy here is genuine and deeply moving.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Morning Chanting Experience</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">One of the most profound experiences at Songzanlin is the <strong>morning chanting ceremony</strong> (6:30 AM daily). Monks gather in the main assembly hall, seated in rows on long cushions, and begin deep, resonant chanting that echoes through the candlelit hall. The sound of Tibetan horns, cymbals, and the collective deep-throat chanting is indescribable.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Visitors are welcome to observe from the sides or back of the hall. <strong>Dress modestly</strong> (cover shoulders and knees), <strong>remove your hat</strong>, and <strong>do not use flash photography</strong>. Sit or stand quietly &mdash; this is a religious ceremony, not a performance. Donations (10&ndash;20 RMB) in the offering box are appreciated but not required.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">How to Get There</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">By Bus</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Take Bus No. 3 from Shangri-La city center. The bus terminates at the monastery parking lot. Fare: <strong>2 RMB</strong>. Buses run every 15&ndash;20 minutes. Journey takes about 20 minutes from the old town area.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Taxi or Didi</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A taxi from Dukezong Old Town costs <strong>15&ndash;25 RMB</strong> (10&ndash;15 minutes). From the new town or airport area, expect <strong>25&ndash;40 RMB</strong>. Taxis are readily available at the monastery for the return trip.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">On Foot (for early morning chanting)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The monastery is a 3 km walk from the northern edge of Dukezong Old Town. Allow 40 minutes. This is the best option for the 6:30 AM chanting if you're staying in the old town &mdash; no buses run that early.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Cultural Etiquette</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Walk <strong>clockwise</strong> around all stupas, prayer wheels, and temple halls.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Do not point <strong>your feet</strong> toward Buddha statues or monks.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Ask permission before photographing monks. Many are happy to oblige, but some will decline.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>No shorts, no sleeveless tops, remove hats inside temple halls.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Do not touch religious artifacts or sit on monks' cushions.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Step <strong>over</strong> the threshold, never on it.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Where to Eat Nearby</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">There is a small Tibetan tea house at the monastery exit serving yak butter tea, sweet tea, and tsampa (10&ndash;20 RMB). For a proper meal, head back to Dukezong Old Town 10 minutes away, where dozens of Tibetan restaurants serve yak hotpot, momo (dumplings), and noodle soups. The monastery is close enough to combine with an afternoon exploring the old town.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-700">Nearby &raquo;</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/attractions/dukezong-old-town" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Dukezong Old Town</a>
      <a href="/attractions/pudacuo-national-park" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Pudacuo National Park</a>
      <a href="/attractions/napa-lake" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Napa Lake</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DetailLayout>
